Tinexus Platform — Licensing Overview
=====================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Abhishek Gour.

Tinexus Platform is an independent, standalone project created and
maintained by Abhishek Gour.

Tinexus Platform uses a per-component licensing split. No single file is
offered under a choice of licenses; the license that applies is determined
by the directory the file lives in, as listed below.

Full license texts:
  - LICENSE-GPL-2.0        GNU General Public License, version 2
  - LICENSE-Apache-2.0     Apache License, version 2.0


1. GPL-2.0-or-later  (SPDX: GPL-2.0-or-later)
---------------------------------------------
Core platform components, daemons and applications. This is the default for
everything not listed under sections 2 or 3.

  src/comp/            Wayland compositor (tinexus-comp)
  src/serviced/        Platform supervisor
  src/ipcd/            IPC broker
  src/searchd/         Search engine
  src/session/         Session lifecycle
  src/settings/        Settings daemon
  src/notifications/   Notification daemon
  src/clipboard/       Clipboard manager
  src/wallpaper/       Wallpaper renderer
  src/shell/           TopBar (tinexus-shell)
  src/dock/            Dock
  src/launcher/        Command palette
  src/lock/            Lock screen
  src/settings-ui/, src/about/, src/files/, src/terminal/, src/monitor/,
  src/login/, src/splash/, src/indexer/, src/guard/, src/displayd/,
  src/pkg/, src/app-installer/, src/iso/, src/liveusb/, src/release/
  tools/, tests/, benchmarks/, examples/ (unless a file states otherwise)


2. Apache-2.0  (SPDX: Apache-2.0)
---------------------------------
SDKs, shared libraries and Tinexus-authored protocol definitions, so that
third-party plugins and applications may link against them freely.

  sdk/                 Plugin SDK
  src/sdk/             SDK headers and build files
  src/common/          Shared C++ libraries (D-Bus names, logging, pools)
  src/txui/            libtxui UI framework
  include/             Public headers
  protocols/tinexus-global-shortcut-v1.xml
  protocols/tinexus-shell-helper-v1.xml


3. Third-party material (own licenses retained)
-----------------------------------------------
The following files are NOT covered by sections 1 or 2. Each keeps the
license stated in its own header:

  protocols/xdg-shell.xml
  protocols/wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1.xml
  protocols/wlr-screencopy-unstable-v1.xml
  protocols/wlr-foreign-toplevel-management-unstable-v1.xml
  protocols/org-kde-kwin-blur.xml
  assets/fonts/            see assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt


Contributions
-------------
Contributions are accepted under the license of the component they modify
(see docs/18_GOVERNANCE.md, section 6: CLA / DCO). Contributors retain
copyright in their own contributions; the project copyright holder is
listed above.
